  "title": "The Printer-Paper Waterfall",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "miniature adventure",
  "premise": "A paper-sized messenger must carry a seal across a desk before a harmless sheet dispenser fills it with blank pages. They surf one outgoing page, leap into its curling edge, and arrive on the destination tray inside a perfectly folded paper pocket.",
  "hook": "The floor arrives one sheet at a time.",
  "visible_action": "Sheets emerge, curl, and stack; messenger slides along a page; one corner folds into a pocket that lands on a tray.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A moving obstacle can sometimes supply the route.",
  "gate": "Use a fictional low-force paper dispenser, never a person inside a real printer or moving machine.",
